    "body": "I'm reopening #1972 since my local repo was messed up and Github closed that ticket\r\n\r\nReplace the monolithic generate-bindings.sh script with a CI-driven swift-publish workflow that builds the XCFramework and syncs sources to the cdk-swift distribution repo. This separates the heavy cross-compilation (iOS device, iOS simulator, macOS universal) from the local development loop.\r\n\r\nLocal changes:\r\n- Rework `ffi-generate-swift` justfile recipe to set up an SPM-compatible package structure (Sources/Cdk, Sources/cdk_ffiFFI) using the dylib from `ffi-build`, enabling `swift test` without building XCFrameworks\r\n- Add `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` to CI and `test-swift` so the dynamic library is found at runtime\r\n- Gate bip353 FFI exports behind `feature = \"bip353\"` to allow the Swift FFI crate to opt out of features that pull in heavy DNS dependencies\r\n- Pin cdk-ffi dependency in Swift crate to only `npubcash` and `bip353` features (no default features) for a leaner build\r\n- Add Swift SPM generated artifacts to .gitignore\r\n- Remove the now-unused `binding-swift` justfile target\r\n- Add bindings/swift/README.md with SPM and Xcode installation docs\r\n- Update bindings/README.md to reflect the new CI-driven build flow\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe the purpose of this PR, what's being adding and/or fixed -->\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\n### Notes to the reviewers\r\n\r\n<!-- In this section you can include notes directed to the reviewers, like explaining why some parts\r\nof the PR were done in a specific way -->\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\n### Suggested [CHANGELOG](https://github.com/cashubtc/cdk/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md) Updates\r\n\r\n<!-- Please do not edit the actual changelog but note what you changed here. -->\r\n\r\n#### CHANGED\r\n\r\n#### ADDED\r\n\r\n#### REMOVED\r\n\r\n#### FIXED\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\n### Checklist\r\n\r\n* [x] I followed the [code style guidelines](https://github.com/cashubtc/cdk/blob/main/CODE_STYLE.md)\r\n* [x] I ran `just quick-check` before committing\r\n* [x] If the Wallet API was modified (added/removed/changed), I have reflected those changes in the FFI bindings (`crates/cdk-ffi`)\r\n",
